  "question": "X2, rule T refit 1 (the margin track's extra width), fresh round: a lone 6 wide Shape on the right margin track (lines 21 to 27), pressed 30% in from its left, held and moved +1, then left in steps, ring read at each, twice (R1, R2), at four frame widths not read before: 1440 and 1560 (margin track under 1.5 columns), 1680 and 1760 (2.2 and 2.9 columns). Gestures Probe, unsaved, one block per enter.",
  "rule": "T refit 1: let p be the column pitch, M the right margin track's width (frame's right edge minus x of line 26), n = 5 + round(M / p) and c = 5 + ceil(M / p), the block's box width in columns rounded and rounded up. If n is 6 or less, the block follows the left edge rule from the first pixel (21 - floor(-dx / p + 0.4) moving left, 21 moving right). Otherwise a move right goes to column 27 - c; a move left is on column 27 - (n + 2) until -(M / 2 + 5), then on 27 - (n + 1), and in both it takes the left edge rule's column when that is further left. At 1600 (M 89.125, p 58.78125: n 7, c 7) this is T as built: 20 at +1, 18, 19 from -49.6, then the left edge rule.",
  "from": "Scratch predictor of refit 1 (columns), fitted on CAP-X2SIX.json (1600, A and B, 18 of 18) and CAP-X2TWIDTHS.json (1280 and 1920, 19 of 19): 37 of 37 seen. The switch at -(M / 2 + 5) is one choice inside the seen gaps (-49 to -50 at 1600, -100 to -148 at 1920); points sit at least 5px from it and from 0.556 M. M and p are ours' computed grid at each width (equal to the oracle's boxes at 1280, 1600 and 1920). asBuilt: ours on main (rule T at every width), from mid-check's hold sweep.",
  "hit": "Each case's two ring reads must agree; then the ring must equal refit 1's area. A start not on 1/21/7/27, or the block not selected, is a setup miss, named, not scored. Two reads that disagree are named unsteady. Refit 1 is built only if it beats asBuilt on these reads.",
